      presentation: "spontaneous-episodic-vertigo-older",
      usage: ["lesson", "review", "challenge"],
      vignette: "A 67-year-old smoker with hypertension and diabetes has had three episodes of spinning vertigo in the past two weeks. Each came on at rest, without any change in position, and lasted 5 to 10 minutes. There was no headache, hearing loss, or tinnitus. He has never had migraine. He feels well now, and his examination, including a Dix-Hallpike test, is normal.",
