      order: [["a", "b"], ["c"], ["d"]],
      rationale: "New headache, [[jaw-claudication|jaw claudication]], [[polymyalgia-rheumatica|polymyalgic]] symptoms, and transient monocular loss in a woman over 50 are [[giant-cell-arteritis|giant cell arteritis]] until proven otherwise. Transient loss is a warning that permanent loss from [[ischemic-optic-neuropathy|arteritic ischemic optic neuropathy]] or retinal artery occlusion may follow. The 2021 ACR guideline recommends prompt high-dose glucocorticoids, intravenous pulse therapy considered when vision is threatened, and a biopsy that does not delay treatment; blood for ESR and CRP is drawn at the same time, not first.",
