      vignette: "A 63-year-old with diabetes, hypertension, and sleep apnea woke this morning with the lower half of the vision in his left eye missing. There is no pain, including on eye movement. Acuity is mildly reduced on the left. There is a left relative afferent pupillary defect, and the left optic disc is swollen with a small hemorrhage at its edge; the right disc is small with little central cup. He has no headache, jaw claudication, or scalp tenderness, and ESR and CRP are normal.",
      stem: "What is the most likely diagnosis?",
