      rationale: "[[ischemic-optic-neuropathy|Ischemic optic neuropathy]] is the commonest acute optic neuropathy in older adults. The nonarteritic form causes sudden painless loss, often on waking, with a swollen disc and an altitudinal field defect; a small crowded fellow disc and vascular risk factors are typical. [[optic-neuritis|Optic neuritis]], as in the Optic Neuritis Treatment Trial population, is painful and occurs in younger adults. In every older patient, exclude [[giant-cell-arteritis|giant cell arteritis]].",
