      "A bedside test that lays the patient back with the head turned to set off positional vertigo.",
      "A provocative test for posterior canal BPPV: with the head turned 45 degrees to one side, the patient is moved from sitting to supine with the neck slightly extended. A positive test produces vertigo with upbeating, torsional nystagmus toward the lower ear, after a brief latency, fading within about a minute.",
