      "Occlusion of the central retinal artery, usually embolic from the carotid artery or heart and sometimes from giant cell arteritis, causing sudden painless severe monocular vision loss with an RAPD, retinal whitening, and a cherry-red spot. A form of acute ischemic stroke that needs emergency stroke evaluation.",
      undefined,
